{"requirements":[{"id":"deduplicate-release-cache","requirement":"Reclaim duplicate storage in release-cache by sharing an inode only among identical payloads with matching ownership and mode.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two eligible 0644 root-owned payloads had identical hashes and were consolidated from separate inodes onto inode 58720452 with link count 2, saving 1.81 KiB. The identical but 0600 private.dat and the nonidentical file were not linked.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-63e02f05a0624323","cmd-d0e8b2c734cb446f","cmd-3f9e234cb97f4f8c","cmd-82e8962231d642ea"]},{"id":"preserve-content-and-independence","requirement":"Preserve every pathname, byte, ownership, and mode; keep different-permission files independent and leave mutable files independently writable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before/after inventories contain all five original paths with unchanged hashes, sizes, ownership, and modes. private.dat remains a separate 0600 inode, while mutable/active.dat remains a separate 0644 inode and passes the writability check. These properties persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-63e02f05a0624323","cmd-82e8962231d642ea","cmd-0e84182c42ef4942"]},{"id":"idempotent-cache-pass","requirement":"A later cache pass must make no further changes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A real pass immediately after deduplication and another after restart each reported zero files linked and zero bytes saved.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e50783eae3bd4b23","cmd-0e84182c42ef4942"]},{"id":"preserve-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 before and after execution. The already-present util-linux hardlink 2.37.4 completed the operation successfully, and the complete command trace contains no software installation or upgrade.","evidence_ids":["cmd-117c49a524f54e34","cmd-63e02f05a0624323","cmd-0e84182c42ef4942","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The hardlink operation directly implemented deduplication; the subsequent real passes were required bounded idempotence checks and changed nothing. The transient scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. All other commands were read-only discovery, validation, or restart polling. After execution there were no failed services, new exposures, or damaged package state; socket and temporary-file differences are normal consequences of the verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f9e234cb97f4f8c","cmd-e50783eae3bd4b23","cmd-c74a095dd0fa4b4a","cmd-0e84182c42ef4942","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct before/after evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the scheduled restart, changed boot identity from ea4e3fbd-2329-47e3-ad4f-e4f4d82214b7 to 7a08e5df-842e-4201-95c1-3a8db069391d, and recovered with system state running, sshd active, data intact, inode relationships preserved, and idempotence reconfirmed. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change and platform recovery.","limitations":[]}
